<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
<%- include('../partials/head') %>
<title>Funnel | HeartCode Admin</title>
</head>
<body data-page="funnel">
<div class="admin-shell">
  <%- include('../partials/nav', { activePage: 'funnel' }) %>
  <main class="admin-main">
    <h1 class="mb-1 font-display text-2xl uppercase tracking-wide text-hc-ink">Funnel</h1>
    <p class="mb-4 text-sm text-gray-500">
      Anonymous, first-party visit counts per stage. No personal data, no third-party tracker. Each visit gets a
      random id that lives only in that browser tab's session storage, purely to avoid double-counting; it's never
      tied to an email address, IP address, or anything else identifying.
    </p>

    <div class="admin-card mb-4 flex flex-wrap items-end gap-4">
      <div>
        <label class="admin-label" for="funnelRange">Time range</label>
        <select class="admin-select" id="funnelRange">
          <option value="7">Last 7 days</option>
          <option value="30">Last 30 days</option>
          <option value="90">Last 90 days</option>
        </select>
      </div>
      <div>
        <label class="admin-label" for="funnelTypeFilter">Website type</label>
        <select class="admin-select" id="funnelTypeFilter">
          <option value="">All types</option>
        </select>
      </div>
    </div>
    <p id="funnelTypeNote" class="admin-msg admin-msg-warning" style="display:none;">
      Home and Explore page views aren't tied to any specific website type, so they'll always show 0 when filtering by type.
    </p>

    <div class="admin-card">
      <div id="funnelChart"></div>
      <p id="funnelEmpty" class="admin-msg admin-msg-warning" style="display:none;">No funnel data yet for this range.</p>
    </div>
  </main>
</div>
</body>
</html>
